\documentclass{article}
\title{Batch Effects in Single-Cell RNA Sequencing}
\author{I. Petrenko}
\date{February 2026}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Normalisation}
Library size varies by orders of magnitude across cells in the same experiment.
\begin{mybox}
We therefore normalise counts with size factors estimated from pooled cells,
and we regress out technical covariates before any clustering is attempted.
\end{mybox}
Downstream embeddings change noticeably when this step is skipped,
and batch structure can be mistaken for biological signal.
\end{document}

